PART 5: CORRECT BINGO NUMBER MARKING AND WINNER VALIDATION

8. Fix Incorrect Winner Verification

Current problem

A card may be declared a winner even if a called number was never marked on that card by the player.

This behavior must be corrected.

A number being called does not automatically mean that the player has marked it.

The application must distinguish between:

Officially called numbers.

Numbers manually marked by the player.

Automatically marked numbers, if the user has explicitly enabled the supported auto-complete feature.

Numbers that are unmarked.

Required marking behavior

For each registered card, maintain a separate marking state.

When an official number is called:

Highlight the number on the 75-number board.

Add the number to the called-number history.

Identify which registered cards contain that number.

Allow the player to mark the corresponding number on each of their cards.

Do not automatically mark the number on every card unless auto-complete is explicitly enabled and its rules permit it.

When the player manually marks a number:

Verify that the number exists on that card.

Verify that the number has already been officially called.

Update the marking state for that card only.

Save the marking state if persistence is required by the current game architecture.

Reflect the change in the UI.

Prevent users from marking numbers that have not been called.

Do not allow a number marked on one card to become marked on another card automatically unless the user has enabled the explicitly supported auto-complete setting.

Winning verification must check two conditions

For a manually marked card, a valid Bingo claim requires both:

Every required number in the selected winning pattern has been officially called.

Every required number in the selected winning pattern has been marked on that specific registered card, unless the explicitly enabled auto-complete feature has already marked it according to the application's rules.

The FREE center space counts as marked.

Do not infer a player's marked state from the official called-number history alone.

Important implementation detail

Use the server's official called-number history to validate that each marked number was eligible to be marked.

Maintain a separate per-card marked-number state and synchronize it with the backend.

At claim time, verify the card's registered number matrix, the official call sequence, the applicable marked-number state, and the active winning pattern.

Do not accept arbitrary marked numbers supplied by the client without validation.

If a player claims Bingo but one or more required numbers remain unmarked, reject the claim and apply the false-claim policy.

Auto-complete setting

The application will include an Auto Complete setting.

When disabled:

Players must manually mark the called numbers on each card.

A called but unmarked number must not count toward a winning pattern.

When enabled:

Automatically mark eligible called numbers on the user's registered cards.

Persist or reliably reconstruct the auto-marked state according to the game's rules.

Ensure that the feature never marks numbers that have not been called.

Display a clear indication that auto-complete is enabled.

The server must validate the selected marking policy rather than trusting a client to claim that auto-complete was active.

Do not silently change a player's marking mode during an active game.

Acceptance tests

Test all of the following:

A called number that is marked correctly counts toward a pattern.

A called number that remains unmarked does not count when auto-complete is disabled.

A number that has not been called cannot be marked.

A number marked on one card does not mark the same number on another card when auto-complete is disabled.

The FREE center space is treated correctly.

A card with all numbers called but an incomplete manual marking pattern is rejected when auto-complete is disabled.

A card with a valid, fully marked pattern can win.

A false claim is rejected and the correct card is blocked.

The result remains consistent after reconnecting or refreshing the application.

